.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-022-goal-history-checkpoints-and-compaction.md:13:Goal: Design durable goal history/checkpoint artifacts that improve reload, compaction, handoff, and auditability without bloating provider context.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-022-goal-history-checkpoints-and-compaction.md:17:`pi-goal` persists compact state and telemetry, but it does not produce durable human-readable checkpoints. Long goals can span compaction, reload, handoffs, and branch navigation. A future maintainer may need a concise timeline: objective changes, subgoals completed, proofs run, blockers, and next action.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-022-goal-history-checkpoints-and-compaction.md:21:- `/goal checkpoint` creates a compact durable checkpoint custom entry or markdown artifact.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-022-goal-history-checkpoints-and-compaction.md:22:- Automatic checkpoints may occur on pause, budget limit, completion, or compaction-adjacent events.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-022-goal-history-checkpoints-and-compaction.md:23:- Checkpoints summarize current goal state, current subgoal, recent proof results, remaining work, and next action.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-022-goal-history-checkpoints-and-compaction.md:24:- Goal history can be viewed/exported without injecting the whole history into every model turn.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-022-goal-history-checkpoints-and-compaction.md:28:1. Should checkpoints live as `pi-goal-state` events, separate custom entries, or files under `.ai/docs` / `.pi-goals`?
